answer:
The Commission identifies seven main elements in the definition of an AI system [ai_system_definition_guidelines, Part II, paras (8)-(10)]:

1. A machine-based system;
2. Designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy;
3. May exhibit adaptiveness after deployment;
4. Operates for explicit or implicit objectives;
5. Infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs;
6. Such as predictions, content, recommendations, or decisions;
7. That can influence physical or virtual environments [ai_system_definition_guidelines, Part II, paras (8)-(10)].

This is a reading of the text, not legal advice.
